---
/**
 * PaneLink.astro — vertical connector between two stacked panes on
 * `/experiencia` (owner request, 2026-09-25: "que se vea que vamos de abajo
 * hacia arriba").
 *
 * The page stacks the panes newest first (Plazasys, Marmibas, then the past
 * roles down to Cleverpy), so the career reads bottom → top. Each link is the
 * same scrolling dashed bar the lock-up connector uses (`.t-flow-v`), with
 * its direction reversed so the dashes travel upward, and a violet "↑" badge
 * styled like `LockupPane`'s "×" badge.
 *
 * It also owns the vertical gap between the two panes it joins, so the panes
 * next to it render with `topSpacingDesktop`/`topSpacingMobile` set to `0`.
 * Reduced motion: `.t-flow-v` is already stopped by `motion.css`; the static
 * dashes and the arrow still convey the direction.
 */
---

<div class="pane-link" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="pane-link__bar t-flow-v"></span>
  <span class="pane-link__arrow">↑</span>
</div>

<style>
  .pane-link {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 88px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .pane-link {
      height: 64px;
    }
  }

  /* Two classes so this beats `.t-flow-v`'s `animation` shorthand
     regardless of stylesheet order. */
  .pane-link__bar.t-flow-v {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 50%;
    width: 2px;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    animation-direction: reverse;
  }

  .pane-link__arrow {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background: var(--bg-0);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--accent-400);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
</style>
